# Supply Method

Grouping column **`Supply Method`** on Custom Label, Plain Database, and Packs. Not the old CL `Warehouse Stock` column (China bags).

Code: `shared/supply_method.py`. One-off: `python scripts/fill_supply_method.py`. Future CL rows: `fill_from_seeds.py --steps supply`.

| Cell | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `Warehouse Stock` | Fruit of the Loom men / women / kids **t-shirts only** |
| `In House Manufacture` | Iron-on or sticker (printed / CL only) |
| `Supplier On Demand` | Gildan t-shirts and everything else |

Decision order:

1. If this is CL **and** Custom Label (SKU) or Gender Apparel contains `iron on` / `ironon` / `iron-on` / `sticker` (spaces and hyphens ignored) → `In House Manufacture`
2. Else if FOTL identity **and** `Category (Areeb)` = `T-SHIRTS` **and** not vest/tank → `Warehouse Stock`
3. Else → `Supplier On Demand`

FOTL identity: Brand contains Fruit + Loom, or Brand/GA `FOTL`/`FOLT`, or GA is `Mens-T-Shirt` / `Womens-T-Shirt` / `Kids-T-Shirt` with blank Brand. **Gildan brand always wins** (on-demand).

Plain / Packs: `allow_in_house=False` — never write `In House Manufacture`.

